menu "Aimless Moving Map"

    config AIMLESS_TILE_BASE
        string "Where remote tiles come from"
        default "https://build.protomaps.com/"
        help
            The directory the remote PMTiles archive is in, ending in a
            slash; the archive's name is appended. src: the original's
            TILE_BASE.

            The default is Protomaps' own build bucket. They ask that it
            not be hotlinked and say its URLs may move: fine for trying
            this, and the reason it is a setting. Any host that answers
            HTTP range requests works -- your own copy on R2, S3, or a
            server at home.

    config AIMLESS_PINNED_BUILD
        string "Pinned build (empty: newest daily)"
        default ""
        help
            An archive name without ".pmtiles" to use as it is, with no
            date probing -- the only sensible setting when the base is
            your own storage. Empty: probe backwards from today's date for
            the newest Protomaps daily build, as the original does.
            src: the original's PINNED_BUILD.

endmenu
